LiquidationPeriphery::setUsm
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when new usm is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when new usm is already set
│   └── it should revert with AlreadySet
├── when new usm stable token differs from BORROW_TOKEN
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
└── when new usm is valid with matching stable token
    ├── it should emit UsmSet
    └── it should update usm
